$ whycant exec /srv/notes.txt

✗ alice (uid 1000) probably cannot exec /srv/notes.txt

  /                drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /srv             drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /srv/notes.txt   -rwxr-xr-x  alice:alice  ✗ exec   ← blocked here

Why
  /srv/notes.txt neither starts with #! nor is an ELF binary, so execve fails with
  "Exec format error". Shells fall back to running such files as sh scripts, so it
  may still work when started from a shell.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Add a #! line naming its interpreter, e.g. #!/bin/sh.
